## When working with Supabase

1. Call tools only on `supabase-thecurtainguy` / `project-0-the-curtain-guy-supabase-thecurtainguy`.
2. Confirm project URL/ref matches `xszhnecwhjcywhqjzfit` when available.
3. Prefer read/list tools before migrations or destructive SQL.
4. Do not create migrations or change Auth unless the user explicitly requests it.

## Migration file naming

Local files must exactly match what the database records, so `supabase/migrations` never needs cleanup.

- After `apply_migration`, call `list_migrations` and name the file `<version>_<name>.sql` using the **exact** version and name returned (e.g. `20261026081529_tcg_customers.sql`).
- Never invent the timestamp locally before applying; the database assigns it.
- New migration names use the `tcg_` prefix and snake_case.
- Before finishing, diff `ls supabase/migrations` against `list_migrations`; both must list the same entries.
